{
  "id": "doc_comp01",
  "meta": {
    "title": "Building with Vanilla Breeze Components",
    "slug": "vanilla-breeze-components",
    "collection": "docs",
    "description": "How VanillaPress block types map to Vanilla Breeze's HTML elements and custom components.",
    "author_id": "author_t1",
    "status": "published",
    "created": "2026-02-14",
    "updated": "2026-04-24",
    "published": "2026-02-14",
    "tags": ["vanilla-breeze", "rendering", "html"]
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        { "type": "text", "value": "VanillaPress stores content as a typed block AST and renders each block to an HTML element that " },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "attrs": { "href": "https://vanilla-breeze.com" },
          "children": [{ "type": "text", "value": "Vanilla Breeze" }]
        },
        { "type": "text", "value": " styles. The block names are stable (callout, tabs, card, code_block); the HTML output tracks VB's vocabulary." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "attrs": { "variant": "tip" },
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            { "type": "text", "value": "VB ships a complete CSS reset, tokens, typography, layout primitives, and ~60 web components. VanillaPress ships zero project-local CSS — the only stylesheet on the page is " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "vanilla-breeze.css", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": "." }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": { "level": 2 },
      "children": [
        { "type": "text", "value": "How a page is assembled" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "step",
          "attrs": { "title": "Author the block AST" },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                { "type": "text", "value": "Each document is a JSON tree of typed blocks defined in " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "src/schema/content-schema.js", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": ". Blocks have a type, optional attrs, and children or a leaf value." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "step",
          "attrs": { "title": "Render to HTML with Vanilla Breeze tags" },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                { "type": "text", "value": "The HTML renderer maps each block to its VB equivalent: callout → " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "<status-message>", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": ", tabs → " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "<tab-set>", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": " (wrapping " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "<details>", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": "), card → " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "<layout-card>", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": ", code_block → " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "<code-block>", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": " (the @profpowell/code-block element)." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "step",
          "attrs": { "title": "Browser upgrades the elements" },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                { "type": "text", "value": "VB's JS module upgrades the custom elements: " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "<tab-set>", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": " becomes a horizontal tab strip with keyboard navigation, " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "<page-info>", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": " synthesizes a provenance panel from meta tags, and so on. Without JS the markup degrades to native HTML." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": { "level": 2 },
      "children": [
        { "type": "text", "value": "Same content, three serializations" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tabs",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "tab",
          "attrs": { "label": "Block AST" },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                { "type": "text", "value": "What the editor stores and the API serves over " },
                { "type": "text", "value": "Accept: application/json", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": ":" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code_block",
              "attrs": { "language": "json" },
              "value": "{\n  \"type\": \"callout\",\n  \"attrs\": { \"variant\": \"warning\" },\n  \"children\": [\n    { \"type\": \"paragraph\",\n      \"children\": [\n        { \"type\": \"text\", \"value\": \"This API is experimental.\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "tab",
          "attrs": { "label": "Vanilla Breeze HTML" },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                { "type": "text", "value": "What renders for a browser request:" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code_block",
              "attrs": { "language": "html" },
              "value": "<status-message data-variant=\"warning\">\n  <div data-content>\n    <p>This API is experimental.</p>\n  </div>\n</status-message>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "tab",
          "attrs": { "label": "Markdown" },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                { "type": "text", "value": "What renders for an LLM request (" },
                { "type": "text", "value": "Accept: text/markdown", "marks": ["code"] },
                { "type": "text", "value": "):" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code_block",
              "attrs": { "language": "markdown" },
              "value": "> **Warning:** This API is experimental."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "attrs": { "variant": "warning" },
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            { "type": "text", "value": "Variant names live in VanillaPress's schema (" },
            { "type": "text", "value": "note", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ", " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "tip", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ", " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "warning", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ", " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "danger", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ") and map to VB's " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "data-variant", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": " values (" },
            { "type": "text", "value": "info", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ", " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "success", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ", " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "warning", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ", " },
            { "type": "text", "value": "error", "marks": ["code"] },
            { "type": "text", "value": ") at render time." }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "collapsible",
      "attrs": { "summary": "Why a typed block AST instead of HTML strings?" },
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            { "type": "text", "value": "Storing HTML couples authoring to one rendering target. A block AST lets the same content render as a full HTML page, an HTML fragment, clean Markdown for LLMs, JSON for APIs, or an Atom entry — all from one source. The schema is the contract; the renderers are pure functions." }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "card",
      "attrs": { "href": "/guides/getting-started/" },
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": { "level": 3 },
          "children": [
            { "type": "text", "value": "Getting Started Guide" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            { "type": "text", "value": "Install Vanilla Press, seed the database, and publish your first page." }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
